  "why": "Around 40 m/min — versus roughly 250 for 6061 aluminium with the same 12 mm carbide end mill: more than a sixfold difference, and stainless wants a heavier per-tooth feed to stay under the work-hardened surface.",
  "context": "Speed drives heat; feed and depth drive cutting force — the heat that should leave in the chip is what cooks a titanium or stainless edge."
};

